---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Gus Mahler"
  description="Personal site of Gus Mahler. Writing on prediction markets, regulation, and political theory."
>
  <main class="about">
    <div class="about__inner">

      <figure class="about__photo">
        <img src="/family.jpg" alt="Me, my parents, and my sister at graduation" width="593" height="600" />
        <figcaption>Me, my parents, and my sister.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <div class="about__text">
        <h1>Who I am &amp; What This Is</h1>
        <div class="about__cols">
          <div class="about__col">
            <p>My name is Gus Mahler, and I recently graduated from Claremont McKenna College with a degree in economics and government. Midway through my senior year, I came to the not-so-novel realization that I should probably get smart on AI if I wanted to find a job. Some months later, I still have no job, but I am smarter on AI, and I'm now using agents to explore the topics and questions I'm interested in.</p>
            <p>I write a weekly newsletter covering the chaotic regulatory landscape facing prediction market companies like Polymarket and Kalshi, and I use multi-agent workflows to automate the sourcing and synthesis stages of the research process.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="about__col">
            <p>I also use AI agents for data collection and cleaning to support analytical research on topics ranging from politics to music.</p>
            <p>I initially began incorporating AI into my daily life and workflows to increase the speed at which I do things, but I now realize that agentic tools have the potential to do much more than that. When used thoughtfully and strategically, tools like Claude Code (my go-to) can dramatically expand both the quality and scope of work.</p>
            <p>Using AI for research still carries a certain taboo, but why should it? I see intentional — and, most importantly, transparent — use of AI as the future, and I'm hoping to show what that can look like here through thoughtful, verifiable, and high-quality work.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="about__foot">
          <a href="/newsletter">Read the newsletter →</a>
          <a href="/thoughts-and-research">Browse thoughts and research →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
